    "https://jobs.wssu.edu/postings/33477": {
      "title": "2027 Sport Management Assistant Professor (Tenure Track)",
      "description": "Winston-Salem State University Employment Opportunities | 2027 Sport Management Assistant Professor (Tenure Track) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help New Hire Forms Compensation Guidelines New Employee Orientation Our Strategic Plan Current WSSU Employee Log in Please use this link to log into PeopleAdmin using the SSO Authentication link. This will log you into the Main Departmental Portal. Scroll down to “My Links” and select Apply Now. This important step will log you into your Application Account that is now tied to your Employee Account. 2027 Sport Management Assistant Professor (Tenure Track) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please Note: A criminal background check will be conducted on candidate finalist prior to the offer of employment. If no applicants apply who meet the required competency and T&E requirements, then management may consider other applicants. Salary would be determined based on competencies, equity, budget, and market considerations. Resumes will not be accepted in lieu of completing an electronic application. The application must be completed in full detail (including work history) for your qualifications to be considered. Failure to complete the application completely may result in you not being considered for the vacant position. Your application for the position will not be complete until you receive an online confirmation number at the end of the process of applying for a position. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at OHR@wssu.edu . Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodation in the application and interview process, please call 336-750-2834 Position Details Classification Information Position Classification Title Assistant Professor FLSA Exempt Position Class (Extract From Banner or PA) 80090 EPA Position Type JCAT 202000 Position Overview Primary Purpose of the Position Faculty in the Department of Health, Physical Education, and Sport Studies at Winston-Salem State University invite applications for a nine-month tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor in Sport Management. This position will begin in August 2027. We seek exceptional candidates with a strong commitment to undergraduate teaching excellence as well as mentoring and advising students inside and outside the classroom. The successful candidate must produce scholarly research that results in publications in peer-reviewed journals. Additionally, the faculty member will facilitate presentations at well-respected professional conferences and engage in the procurement of extramural funds with interdisciplinary teams. We particularly welcome applications from candidates with interests in working collaboratively to enhance the strengths of curricular and co-curricular programs across the arts, humanities, social sciences, business, and education. Position Information Working Position Title 2027 Sport Management Assistant Professor (Tenure Track) Building and Room No. Anderson Center 143A Appointment Type Permanent Full-Time If Time Limited. No Appointment Length. 9 Months Position Number 000134 Requirements and Preferences Position required to work during periods of adverse weather or other emergencies No Normal Work Schedule Monday-Friday, Normal Class Times Department Required Skills We seek exceptional candidates who demonstrate a commitment to excellence in teaching Sport Management to undergraduate students from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. The following qualifications and skills are required for this position, Applicant Must: Have a doctoral degree in Sport Management or a related discipline from a regionally accredited four-year institution of higher education. Provide evidence of mentoring students through experiential learning with a focus in Sport Management. Have the ability to participate in interdisciplinary teaching and research collaborations at the university, across universities, or within the broader community. Demonstrate the ability to participate in interdisciplinary teaching and research collaborations with professional colleagues at the university, across universities, or within the broader public. Demonstrate experience in the sport industry and an ability to work collaboratively with colleagues to enhance curricular and co-curricular programs. Illustrate a commitment to their professional growth and development via engagement in professional organizations and professional conferences. Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education Faculty in the Department of Health, Physical Education, and Sport Studies prefer candidates who: Have experience teaching and enhancing curriculum. Have experience in program assessment. Have leadership experience within professional organizations. Required License or Certification Valid US Driver's License Yes Commercial Driver's License Required No Physical Required No List any other medical/drug tests required Primary Responsibilities and Duties Primary Responsibilities and Duties Describe the specific job duties related to this competency We seek a committed and engaged faculty member who will perform specific duties at a high level. These duties include, but are not limited to the following: Teaching and Mentoring The successful candidate will: Teach Sport Management courses primarily face-to-face, but should have the ability to teach in online and hybrid formats. Construct detailed course syllabi. Facilitate high-quality, engaging instruction. Leverage various technologies (e.g., Canvas, EAB Navigate) to communicate regularly with students, monitor student progress, and provide feedback on student success outcomes. Engage with students during mandatory office hours each week. Work collaboratively to enhance the strengths of our Sport Management curricular and co-curricular programs. Percentage Of Time 100 Posting Details Posting Details Internal Posting Only No Position Type EHRA Non Faculty Time Limited Position No Appointment Length 9 Months Salary Commensurate with Experience Open Date 09/15/2026 Close Date 01/15/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary Please Note: A criminal background check will be conducted on candidate finalist prior to the offer of employment. If no applicants apply who meet the required competency and T&E requirements, then management may consider other applicants. Salary would be determined based on competencies, equity, budget, and market considerations. Resumes will not be accepted in lieu of completing an electronic application. The application must be completed in full detail (including work history) for your qualifications to be considered. Failure to complete the application completely may result in you not being considered for the vacant position. Your application for the position will not be complete until you receive an online confirmation number at the end of the process of applying for a position. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at OHR@wssu.edu . Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodation in the application and interview process, please call 336-750-2834 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Document Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy Unofficial Transcripts Letter of Reference 1 Letter of Reference 2 Letter of Reference 3 References List Optional Documents Winston-Salem State University 601 S. Martin Luther King Jr. Drive Winston-Salem, NC 27110 © 2022 Winston-Salem State University. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.wssu.edu/postings/33474": {
      "title": "2026-2027 Business Administration Faculty (Pooled)",
      "description": "Winston-Salem State University Employment Opportunities | 2026-2027 Business Administration Faculty (Pooled) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help New Hire Forms Compensation Guidelines New Employee Orientation Our Strategic Plan Current WSSU Employee Log in Please use this link to log into PeopleAdmin using the SSO Authentication link. This will log you into the Main Departmental Portal. Scroll down to “My Links” and select Apply Now. This important step will log you into your Application Account that is now tied to your Employee Account. 2026-2027 Business Administration Faculty (Pooled) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please Note: A criminal background check will be conducted on candidate finalist prior to the offer of employment. If no applicants apply who meet the required competency and T&E requirements, then management may consider other applicants. Salary would be determined based on competencies, equity, budget, and market considerations. Resumes will not be accepted in lieu of completing an electronic application. The application must be competed in full detail (including work history) for your qualifications to be considered. Failure to complete the application completely may result in you not being considered for the vacant position. Your application for the position will not be complete until you receive an online confirmation number at the end of the process of applying for a position. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at OHR@wssu.edu . Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodation in the application and interview process, please call 336-750-2834 Position Details Classification Information Position Classification Title FLSA Exempt Position Class (Extract From Banner or PA) 99999 EPA Position Type Faculty JCAT Position Overview Primary Purpose of the Position To meet the growing demand, the College of Business & Entrepreneurship will be adding Adjunct Instructors, specifically in the Department of Business Administration . These Adjunct Instructors may be needed to teach undergraduate courses in Business Communications, Entrepreneurship, Management, Marketing, Management Information Systems, Operations Management, Business Analytics and related fields for the 2026-2027 academic year. This position is a non-tenure track, part-time appointment. Primary Function of Organizational Unit Position Information Working Position Title 2026-2027 Business Administration Faculty (Pooled) Building and Room No. R.J. Reynolds Business Building Room 203 Appointment Type Time limited If Time Limited. Yes Appointment Length. 1-2 Semesters Position Number AJC138 Requirements and Preferences Position required to work during periods of adverse weather or other emergencies No Minimum Experience/Education Master’s Degree or higher from an accredited college or university. A minimum of 18 graduate credit hours in Business Administration, Entrepreneurship, Business Communications, Management, Marketing, Information Systems, Data Sciences, Decision Sciences, Operations Management, Operations Research, Statistics, or related fields. Professional experience in the subject area is preferred. Professional certification or significant current experience may be acceptable in some cases. Excellent interpersonal, oral, and written communication skills. The ability to work effectively with students, faculty, staff, and diverse populations. Normal Work Schedule Weekly with designated class times Monday through Friday. Courses may be scheduled in-person, on-line synchronous, or on-line asynchronous. They are taught over 8-week sessions or over a full 15-week semester. Full-semester courses meet either in-person, synchronously on-line or asynchronously on-line. Synchronous courses typically meet three hours per week between 8am and 8:30pm. Eight-week courses are typically taught asynchronously online and provide similar learning experiences and objectives as full-semester courses in a more intensive compressed timeframe. Must be available for office hours – a minimum of 2 hours per week for full-semester courses and 4 hours per week for eight-week courses. Department Required Skills Successful candidates must adhere to the mission of the University and College. Must have strong communication and instructional skills. Must be able to deliver course content aligned with institutional standards. Must be able to effectively teach assigned classes, grade assignments, provide timely student feedback, ensure learning objectives are attained, and post grades adhering to university deadlines and policies. The ability to successfully teach one or more business-related courses. Must be able to use and work from a course syllabus. Grades and record-keeping using the Canvas system is required. Candidates should be proficient with current technologies and teaching with various tools such as videoconferencing, publisher platforms, and presentation software. Candidates must have a dedication to providing a positive and high-quality learning environment. Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education At least one year of teaching experience at college level. Practical experience in business and entrepreneurship, especially in the area of instruction. Demonstrated skills in classroom management and successful correspondence with students, faculty, staff, and administration. Doctoral degrees and master’s degrees from AACSB accredited programs are preferred. Required License or Certification None Valid US Driver's License No Commercial Driver's License Required No Physical Required No List any other medical/drug tests required None Primary Responsibilities and Duties Primary Responsibilities and Duties Describe the specific job duties related to this competency Adjunct faculty will: Teach assigned classes. Ensure course and program learning outcomes are delivered as defined by the syllabus. Maintain office hours (a way for students to contact and receive guidance from the faculty members) for at least 30 hours per course (2 hours per week for full-semester courses or 4 hours per week for 8-week courses.) Grade assignments, provide feedback to students, and post grades while adhering to relevant university policies. Suitably challenge, engage, serve, and communicate with students to encourage their participation and learning while maintaining mutual respect. Complete grade books, mid-term and final grade submissions, learning assessments (if needed), and final exam assessments on a timely basis. Respond to student questions in a timely manner. Percentage Of Time 100 Posting Details Posting Details Internal Posting Only No Position Type Faculty Time Limited Position Yes Appointment Length 1-2 Semesters Salary Salary is commensurate with experience and academic credentials. Open Date 09/25/2026 Close Date 01/10/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary Please Note: A criminal background check will be conducted on candidate finalist prior to the offer of employment. If no applicants apply who meet the required competency and T&E requirements, then management may consider other applicants. Salary would be determined based on competencies, equity, budget, and market considerations. Resumes will not be accepted in lieu of completing an electronic application. The application must be competed in full detail (including work history) for your qualifications to be considered. Failure to complete the application completely may result in you not being considered for the vacant position. Your application for the position will not be complete until you receive an online confirmation number at the end of the process of applying for a position. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at OHR@wssu.edu . Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodation in the application and interview process, please call 336-750-2834 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Could you describe your educational background, professional experience, and other experience that relates to the subject matter you expect to teach? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Document Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Unofficial Transcript References List Optional Documents Teaching Philosophy Other Document Letter of Reference 1 Letter of Reference 2 Letter of Reference 3 Portfolio Winston-Salem State University 601 S. Martin Luther King Jr. Drive Winston-Salem, NC 27110 © 2022 Winston-Salem State University. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
